<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Pathway xmlns="http://pathvisio.org/GPML/2021" title="divinyl ether biosynthesis II" organism="cellular organisms" source="PlantCyc" version="20260304101735">
  <Description>The divinyl ethers |FRAME: CPD-8679| and |FRAME: CPD-8680| are known plant defense compounds, reported from a few solanaceae species including tomato, potato and tobacco. They are produced by the concerted activities of |FRAME: MONOMER-12726| (9-LOX) and |FRAME: MONOMER-12728| (9-DES) from |FRAME: LINOLEIC_ACID| and |FRAME: LINOLENIC_ACID| (see |FRAME: PWY-5406|). In addition to these two well known divinyl ethers, divinyl ethers that are produced by |FRAME: MONOMER-12736| and |FRAME: MONOMER-12737|, such as |FRAME: CPD-8690|, have been reported from garlic |CITS: [8690066]|.</Description>
  <Authors>
    <Author name="AU4FS-1" />
    <Author name="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE" />
    <Author name="zhang" />
  </Authors>
